1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,797
How do YouTubers actually make money? It's not just ads.

2
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:12,854
To earn from ads, you join the YouTube Partner Program. Usually a thousand subscribers and four thousand public watch hours in a year.

3
00:00:13,204 --> 00:00:17,528
Or a thousand subscribers and ten million Shorts views in ninety days.

4
00:00:17,878 --> 00:00:23,671
On long videos, creators keep about fifty five percent of the ad money their videos bring in.

5
00:00:24,021 --> 00:00:30,836
Shorts work differently. Ad money goes into a shared pool, and creators keep forty five percent of their share.

6
00:00:31,186 --> 00:00:36,580
For a lot of creators, the bigger money comes from sponsors, where brands pay for a mention.

7
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,818
The smartest creators never rely on just one income stream.
